; soft-weak-skin-side.ink on 0.5 mm cells: here master reads the skin too (its cell's peak read lands in the skin), so both answer wrongly; on 1 mm cells only the commit does.
; A 100 x 10 x 10 beam bent by a couple of about 9000 N mm (beam theory: 54 MPa at
; its top and bottom faces, about 4.6 against its yield of 250). A skin 0.1 mm thick
; on its side face y 4.9..5 (z 4..4.8, |x| < 40) is of a much softer, weaker material
; (E 200, yield 25). Along the beam the strain is shared, so the skin carries
; E_skin / E times the stress beside it: about 0.05 MPa, a factor of about 500 there.
; True minimum: about 4.6, at the top and bottom faces.
; truth: safe holds about 2.7 (the beam with one yield, yield-soft-skin-one-yield: 2.71 on 0.5 mm cells, converging; the skin itself carries E_skin / E of the stress beside it, a factor near 500)
; truth: unsafe fails about 2.7 (as safe)
(import "std")
(def part (box 100 10 10))
(def skin (max (- 4.9 y) (- y 5.5) (- 4 z) (- z 4.8) (- (abs x) 40)))
(study s (shape part)
 (elastic (E (* 1MPa (select skin 200 200000))) (nu 0.3) (yield (* 1MPa (select skin 25 250))))
 (fix root (+ x 49))
 (load top (force 1000N 0 0) (region (max (- 49 x) (- 4 z))))
 (load bottom (force -1000N 0 0) (region (max (- 49 x) (+ z 4))))
 (res 0.5))
(require safe (min-safety-factor s > 1))
(require unsafe (min-safety-factor s < 1))
